      "side": 1,
      "message": "although! thinking about it again this morning, the object vector may be better than the linked list because:\n - total memory consumption is less. It is 1 ptr per object vs 2 (prev+next). There is a separate allocation per object type, but perhaps this is not so bad\n - can eventually better support concurrent insertion + deletion if we have some fancy containers for the free id list and object list. would work so long we have some atomics that incr/decr within the resize capacity of the vector. Then, creation/deletion locks only when a resize of the vector(s) is necessary.",
